\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Look your Saviour, the Son of God
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Look at him that He's hanging on the cross
\par See how he is bleeding and dying,
\par  and therefore think of His wonderful love
\par What a friend has done such like him?
\par should one even to die for evil men?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Our Master! What a calamity?
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 You were restless; what a sordid distress
\par And your blood thus flowed from all your wounds
\par and poured out to pacify God for us
\par it is still speaking and to comfort me
\par that my deliverance is pleasing to God.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For, thus it was already ordained
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj that God would provide the offering lamb
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 for the forgiveness of all our sins
\par that made God's Son to be a mediator
\par This is the extent to which God loves men
\par His only Son came and died to save them.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. My Saviour, l greatly do thank you
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj I will follow you and serve you always
\par A day when I, with those in heaven
\par be able to praise you forevermore
\par all the heavenly host will become one
\par to sing our Saviour and Redeemer's praise.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

